  "historical_output_text": " \n\nIn high school, I was on the debate team. During one particular competition, I was paired with a new teammate, Alex. We were to argue for the affirmative side on a motion about reducing class sizes. I was tasked with delivering the opening speech. \n\nI arrived at the debate that day feeling quite confident. I had practiced my opening speech countless times and was sure I could win the judges over. But as the moderator called us to the stage, I noticed Alex was fidgeting nervously. He had a nervous habit of biting his nails, something I had never seen him do before. \n\nI dismissed it as just nervousness, and began my opening remarks. I delivered them smoothly and with conviction. As I finished, I looked over at Alex who had been staring at the floor the entire time. \n\nIn the debriefing after the round, the coach",
